    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a and b rearrange the conditional-probability formula to find P(B) and P(A) from given numeric values. Part c links these through the addition rule, then a complement, to reach P(A'∩B'). This is a multi-step chain linking conditional probability, union and complement. It is somewhat more than p35-q9, which has a small Venn context. It is clearly below p42-q26, which is the same structure but symbolic in p and also asks for an interval for p.",
